<p>The platform covers the full email marketing stack: list building with landing pages and sign-up forms, broadcast email campaigns, automated follow-up sequences, behavioral tagging, and detailed analytics. It's not trying to be a CRM or an all-in-one business platform — it's focused on email, and it does email extremely well.</p>

<h2 id='our-experience'>🧪 Our Experience Testing AWeber with Real Gyms</h2>

<p>Our team embedded AWeber into three different fitness businesses over a six-month testing period: a 1,200-member commercial gym, a boutique cycling studio running 40+ weekly classes, and an independent personal training business with a mix of in-person and online clients.</p>

<p>Across all three, setup time from account creation to first automated campaign sent was under two hours — including importing existing member lists and building a basic welcome sequence. For the cycling studio specifically, we built a class-fill automation that triggered a "spots still open" email 48 hours before underbooked sessions. Within 90 days, average class fill rate improved from 71% to 84%. That one automation, built in about 45 minutes, generated measurable revenue impact.</p>

<p>The deliverability held strong throughout — we tracked open rates between 31% and 47% across different segments, well above the fitness industry average of roughly 22-25%. AWeber's maintained sender reputation and built-in spam testing clearly made a difference.</p>

