<h2 id='how-to-get-started'>🚀 How to Get Started with AWeber as a Gym Owner</h2>

<p>Getting your first campaign live is simpler than most gym operators expect. Here's the sequence we use when onboarding a new fitness business onto AWeber:</p>

<p><strong>1. Create your free account</strong> and import your existing member list from your gym management software (most platforms export to CSV). AWeber's import wizard is clean and handles duplicate detection automatically.</p>

<p><strong>2. Build your welcome sequence first.</strong> A three-email onboarding series — sent on day 1, day 3, and day 7 after someone joins your list — sets the tone for every member relationship. Cover what they can expect from your emails, introduce your facility and team, and include one clear call to action (book a class, schedule a PT consultation, download your onboarding guide).</p>

<p><strong>3. Set up your first broadcast.</strong> Don't overthink it. Pick a fitness-specific template, write a genuine message about something happening at your gym this week, and send it to your full list. The data you get back — who opens, who clicks, who ignores — is immediately actionable for segmentation.</p>

<p><strong>4. Build your win-back automation.</strong> Tag members who haven't opened an email in 60 days and run a three-step re-engagement sequence. If they don't open by email three, suppress them from your main list to protect your sender score.</p>

